1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,400
To prove he was a forger, he had to paint another one.

2
00:00:04,140 --> 00:00:08,520
Let's back up. It's nineteen forty-five, and the war in Europe just ended.

3
00:00:09,540 --> 00:00:13,100
Investigators are searching the art collection of Hermann Goering, a Nazi leader.

4
00:00:13,560 --> 00:00:16,980
And they find a Vermeer, a famous Dutch master from the sixteen hundreds.

5
00:00:18,660 --> 00:00:21,760
Goering paid one point six five million guilders for it.

6
00:00:22,220 --> 00:00:26,080
Guilders were Dutch money back then. So who sold him a Dutch treasure?

7
00:00:26,660 --> 00:00:28,980
Then they trace it to a painter, Han van Meegeren.

8
00:00:29,500 --> 00:00:32,080
Tap the heart if you think he's in deep trouble.

9
00:00:32,660 --> 00:00:35,820
Now he's arrested for collaboration, which means helping the enemy.

10
00:00:36,300 --> 00:00:40,620
And that's when he drops the bomb. That's not a Vermeer. I painted it.

11
00:00:41,020 --> 00:00:45,480
Turns out, for years, he'd been faking Vermeers and selling them as lost discoveries.

12
00:00:46,160 --> 00:00:50,060
Real Vermeers are so rare, experts wanted to believe a new one turned up.

13
00:00:50,460 --> 00:00:53,420
Send this to the friend who'd confess to anything to get out of trouble.

14
00:00:53,940 --> 00:00:56,420
But here's the problem. Nobody believes him.

15
00:00:56,760 --> 00:00:59,660
So he says, fine, give me a canvas, and watch.

16
00:01:00,440 --> 00:01:04,160
Then, with officials watching, he paints a brand-new fake Vermeer.

17
00:01:04,640 --> 00:01:08,140
Wait, so a Nazi leader got scammed with a fake? Yep.

18
00:01:08,780 --> 00:01:11,740
Now the charge switches to forgery, which means faking art.

19
00:01:12,220 --> 00:01:14,960
Follow if you love when a con man cons his way out.

20
00:01:15,380 --> 00:01:18,480
In nineteen forty-seven, he was sentenced to one year in prison.

21
00:01:19,020 --> 00:01:21,700
He died just weeks later, before serving any of it.

22
00:01:22,060 --> 00:01:25,880
He went from traitor to faker, and faker was actually the better deal.

23
00:01:26,460 --> 00:01:28,920
So, genius or crook? One word.

